  "details": "Build 801 has unfairly marked a lot of avatars as 'very poor', namely Pikapetey's Ugandan Shiba which was ranked 'medium' and performed very well. Since Unity cannot check into animators at runtime, allow avatar creators to submit their avatars for review should they be marked 'very poor'.\n\nThe avatars marked unfairly typically have hidden components that increase polygon/ mesh count because now the game assumes worst case. To reign in with the unfair judgement, please allow avatar creators to submit their very poor avatars for review. If they are found to perform adequately even with animations, allow the reviewers to rank the avatars 'poor' at least or give a new 'verified avatar' rank or icon that makes them 'poor' at minimum. With this we can keep malicious/ poor performance avatars in check without removing the minimum displayed performance rank feature or reverting the current way avatars are ranked.\n\nAs for the question of who, either someone from the VRChat team or someone from the community that can be called an \"avatar tester\" can take on the task of reviewing 'very poor' avatars.",
